---
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import SectionHeader from "../components/SectionHeader.astro";
import SiteLayout from "../layouts/SiteLayout.astro";

const commitments = [
  [
    "A complete public product boundary",
    "Gateway, registry, policy, identity, audit, analytics, portability, and self-hosted deployment capabilities stay public as their pre-1.0 implementations mature.",
  ],
  [
    "No license server",
    "Self-hosted operation never requires a cloud account, activation server, or call-home path.",
  ],
  [
    "Portable state",
    "Configuration export exists in preview; complete cross-target import and execution remains an acceptance gate.",
  ],
  [
    "Open compatibility",
    "SDKs, gateway fixtures, and the named-client matrix are public; no named client is marked verified without a recorded run.",
  ],
  [
    "Visible security process",
    "The disclosure policy and limitations are public; signed releases, revocation feeds, and supported release lines remain planned.",
  ],
  [
    "Optional telemetry",
    "The current slice has no telemetry exporter; any future self-hosted export must be opt-in and documented field by field.",
  ],
];
---

<SiteLayout title="Open source" description="LiteMCP Composer defines its complete self-hosted product boundary under Apache 2.0. The implementation is pre-1.0 and call-home-free; the optional operated service has a separate private control plane.">
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Open-source commitment"
    title="The product stays open. The operated service is separate."
    description="LiteMCP Composer is licensed under Apache 2.0. Security, identity, policy, audit, analytics, portability, high-availability, and on-prem capabilities mature in public. Private code is limited to operating our hosted service: customer lifecycle, billing, support access, provisioning, and fleet releases."
    signal="Complete public boundary · pre-1.0 implementation"
  >
    <Fragment slot="actions">
      <a class="button button--primary button--large" href="https://github.com/reachjalil/liteMCP">View GitHub ↗</a>
      <a class="button button--large" href="/docs/getting-started#five-minute-proof">Run the proof locally</a>
      <a class="button button--large" href="https://github.com/reachjalil/liteMCP/blob/main/docs/release-and-lts-policy.md">Release policy ↗</a>
    </Fragment>
  </PageHero>

  <section class="content-section">
    <div class="shell">
      <SectionHeader
        eyebrow="Project covenant"
        title="Portable by architecture and policy—not by maturity claims."
        description="The self-hosted product is independently operable without private code, a license server, a cloud account, or a hosted-service dependency. Live Kubernetes, recovery, and cross-target exit tests are still pending."
      />
      <div class="feature-grid">
        {commitments.map(([title, description], index) => (
          <article class="feature-card">
            <span class="feature-card__index">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span>
            <h3>{title}</h3>
            <p>{description}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--subtle">
    <div class="shell split-layout">
      <div class="split-layout__aside">
        <p class="eyebrow">Governance</p>
        <h2>Trust needs a public operating record.</h2>
        <p>
          The project is being established with a public roadmap, contribution process,
          security policy, release notes, and a maintainer path. Foundation governance can be
          evaluated after meaningful ecosystem participation exists.
        </p>
      </div>
      <ul class="principle-list">
        <li><span>01</span><div><strong>Public roadmap</strong><p>Priorities, validation gates, and known limitations are visible.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>02</span><div><strong>Reviewable releases</strong><p>Signed manifests, checksums, SBOMs, and rollback notes are release gates, not current artifacts.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>03</span><div><strong>Contributor credit</strong><p>Connector and core contributors retain visible attribution and a maintainer path.</p></div></li>
        <li><span>04</span><div><strong>No payload economy</strong><p>Diagnostics do not require customer tool arguments or responses.</p></div></li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="content-section content-section--tight">
    <div class="shell cta-panel">
      <div>
        <h2>Inspect the architecture, then help prove the exit test.</h2>
        <p>Portability is achieved only when a cloud-exported configuration executes on the self-hosted target without proprietary conversion; that live test is still pending.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="cta-panel__actions">
        <a class="button button--primary" href="/docs/self-hosting">Self-hosting guide</a>
        <a class="button" href="/security">Security model</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
